# Cloudflare Pages security headers.
# Applied at the edge — no zone-level API permission required, which matters because the
# Cloudflare token in .env is scoped to Pages only (zone settings return 9109 Unauthorized).
#
# Why these exist: the site redirected HTTP->HTTPS correctly and had a valid certificate, but
# sent NO Strict-Transport-Security header. Without HSTS a browser can still be downgraded to
# plain HTTP on a later request, which is a legitimate "not secure" finding.
#
# NOTE ON `preload`: deliberately NOT set. Preload is a hard, slow-to-reverse commitment via
# hstspreload.org. max-age + includeSubDomains gives the protection without that lock-in.
# Add `; preload` only as a deliberate decision with eyes open.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()

  # CSP verified against the real page first: the site loads NO external scripts and NO web
  # fonts -- only outbound <a href> links, which CSP does not govern. It does use one inline
  # <style> and one inline <script>, hence 'unsafe-inline' for those two directives only.
  # img-src allows data: because the portrait/cover art may be inlined.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'